## Finding the First Negative Number Index

### Function Implementation

```javascript
/**
 * Returns the index of the first negative number in an array.
 * @param {number[]} arr - The input array of numbers
 * @returns {number} The index of the first negative number, or -1 if none found
 */
function findFirstNegativeIndex(arr) {
  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] < 0) {
      return i;
    }
  }
  return -1; // Return -1 if no negative number is found
}
```

### Usage Examples

```javascript
// Basic example with a negative number present
console.log(findFirstNegativeIndex([3, 7, -2, 5, -8]));  // Output: 2

// Negative number at the beginning
